---
import TVLayout from '../layouts/TVLayout.astro'
---

<TVLayout>
  <article class="bio">
    <h1 class="sr-only">Likith Shetty — AI/ML Engineer in Bengaluru</h1>
    <p class="big-text">
      Hi! I'm <span class="bio__photo" tabindex="0">Likith Shetty</span>, based in
      <span class="keep-together"
        ><button class="button-text js-channel-trigger" data-channel="9"
          >Bengaluru</button
        >.</span
      > I'm currently pursuing an M.Sc. in AI and Machine Learning at
      <a
        href="https://christuniversity.in"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">CHRIST University</a
      >, and I build agents, retrieval systems and the occasional optimizer.
      <br /><br />Most of what I make ends up on
      <a
        href="https://github.com/LikithSh3tty"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a
      >, and the whole list is <a href="/open-source/">here</a>. The ones I've
      deployed are <a href="/websites/">live</a>.
      <br /><br />I like systems that admit when they don't know something. They
      would rather tell you they aren't sure than guess at an answer. Some of
      them run retrieval on a model small enough to live inside the function,
      which costs nothing per query and never phones anyone. I wrote about
      <a href="/writing/why-small-language-models-might-be-the-future/"
        >why small models might be the future</a
      > if that sounds like an odd choice; the rest of the
      <a href="/writing/">writing</a> is over here.
      <br /><br />Most recently I was an AI intern at
      <a
        href="https://ontaraai.solutions/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Ontara AI</a
      >, building retrieval pipelines and agent workflows that went into
      client-facing products. Before that I interned at
      <a
        href="https://www.paynearby.in/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">PayNearby</a
      > in Mumbai and led the IT Club at Nitte University. There's a
      <a href="/resume/">resume</a> if you want the long version.
      <br /><br />Almost none of it gets written in silence. Here are the
      <a href="/playlists/">playlists</a> if you want them.
      <br /><br />If you'd like to chat, reach me by
      <a href="mailto:likithshetty188@gmail.com">e-mail</a> or on
      <a
        href="https://linkedin.com/in/likith-shetty"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>
</TVLayout>

<style>
  /* A <button> is an atomic inline, so the browser may break between it and
     the punctuation that follows, orphaning the full stop on the next line. */
  .keep-together {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .bio__photo {
    position: relative;
    color: var(--text-secondary);

    &::after {
      content: '';
      display: block;
      position: absolute;
      z-index: var(--layer-me-hover);
      top: calc(100% + 1em);
      left: 1rem;
      width: 14rem;
      padding-bottom: 14rem;
      visibility: hidden;
      background-size: cover;
    }

    &:hover::after,
    &:focus::after {
      background-image: url(/assets/images/me.png);
      transition: visibility 0s 0.2s;
      visibility: visible;
    }
  }
</style>
